1
00:00:07,125 --> 00:00:07,958
ARCADE

2
00:00:08,041 --> 00:00:11,083
BEFORE GERALD CHEN DISAPPEARED

3
00:00:11,166 --> 00:00:13,875
The professor's theory
is fundamentally flawed.

4
00:00:13,958 --> 00:00:16,416
I've discussed it in the report.
You nearly finished?

5
00:00:24,208 --> 00:00:25,041
Right.

6
00:00:25,125 --> 00:00:26,333
SPECIAL OFFER ON TOKENS, 404

7
00:00:26,416 --> 00:00:30,041
Uh, I'll get it to you
before 10:00. See you.

8
00:01:12,916 --> 00:01:16,583
I forgot my power cord.
I'll see you back at school.

9
00:01:30,666 --> 00:01:31,958
Don't move.

10
00:01:32,750 --> 00:01:34,208
Move and I kill you.

11
00:01:35,291 --> 00:01:37,083
Knifing me from that angle?

12
00:01:37,166 --> 00:01:39,833
My grandma could do better.
What do we need you for?

13
00:01:44,333 --> 00:01:46,500
Never forget what could be behind you.

14
00:01:47,208 --> 00:01:48,500
Keep up your training.

15
00:01:49,916 --> 00:01:52,416
It was Ben's voice that exposed you.

16
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:54,250
-Try again next time.
-Try again?

17
00:01:54,333 --> 00:01:56,833
Let me make my will first.

18
00:01:58,833 --> 00:02:00,625
Why'd you make such a mess here?

19
00:02:00,708 --> 00:02:03,666
You were gone
for three or four months straight.

20
00:02:03,750 --> 00:02:04,958
Can't you reply to messages?

21
00:02:07,125 --> 00:02:08,666
You still wear this?

22
00:02:10,250 --> 00:02:12,625
Uh, no. I just haven't thrown it out.

23
00:02:13,833 --> 00:02:14,833
You want it?

24
00:02:20,291 --> 00:02:21,208
Mina…

25
00:02:23,375 --> 00:02:25,000
you were careless before.

26
00:02:25,583 --> 00:02:28,666
Whatever you're in,
you must have a way out.

27
00:02:29,416 --> 00:02:30,291
Hear me?

28
00:02:32,708 --> 00:02:33,875
Got it.

29
00:02:36,250 --> 00:02:37,916
And…

30
00:02:40,958 --> 00:02:41,875
happy birthday.

31
00:02:51,916 --> 00:02:55,375
I don't celebrate my birthday.
Stop singing! It's embarrassing.

32
00:02:55,458 --> 00:02:57,291
I can't sing, then make a wish.

33
00:02:57,375 --> 00:02:59,291
I don't want to. It's all bull.

34
00:02:59,375 --> 00:03:01,083
You are such a child.

35
00:03:01,166 --> 00:03:04,291
Don't be such a downer.
Come on, make a wish.

36
00:03:07,208 --> 00:03:08,875
Try, will you?

37
00:03:26,375 --> 00:03:28,291
THE FIXERS

38
00:03:45,958 --> 00:03:49,333
TIEN-BU-LA

39
00:03:54,250 --> 00:03:55,750
Don't get in the car.

40
00:03:59,041 --> 00:04:00,250
Hey, you're…

41
00:04:00,750 --> 00:04:02,166
How did William die?

42
00:04:02,750 --> 00:04:03,875
You should be careful.

43
00:04:05,458 --> 00:04:07,083
You were so close to him.

44
00:04:08,333 --> 00:04:10,166
Do you think that you'll be spared?

45
00:04:20,791 --> 00:04:22,750
Why the interest in Zoe?

46
00:04:23,416 --> 00:04:26,500
Anyone who's connected to Zoe
will end up like William.

47
00:04:26,583 --> 00:04:29,208
You don't think
he took his own life, do you?

48
00:04:29,708 --> 00:04:31,125
I don't know.

49
00:04:31,625 --> 00:04:34,916
If you wanna stay alive,
you need to tell us everything.

50
00:04:36,416 --> 00:04:38,666
All I know is Zoe left the company

51
00:04:39,166 --> 00:04:42,125
because she found out
William was moving Yuan Tao's funds

52
00:04:42,208 --> 00:04:44,166
to invest in Tolita behind her back

53
00:04:44,250 --> 00:04:45,500
to commit fraud.

54
00:04:45,583 --> 00:04:47,208
Was he the reason she died?

55
00:04:47,291 --> 00:04:49,541
William panicked when he found out.

56
00:04:49,625 --> 00:04:51,125
And it wasn't an act.

57
00:04:51,666 --> 00:04:53,708
You know what happened to Zoe's husband.

58
00:04:53,791 --> 00:04:56,166
Zoe died a week after
he took his own life.

59
00:04:56,250 --> 00:04:57,500
If you believe that.

60
00:05:01,416 --> 00:05:03,583
The day Hsu Ming-yi died,
he called William.

61
00:05:03,666 --> 00:05:04,708
And then?

62
00:05:04,791 --> 00:05:08,625
William seemed very nervous
when he picked up. He said,

63
00:05:09,750 --> 00:05:11,416
"Where did you hear that?"

64
00:05:12,125 --> 00:05:13,833
"They're not to be messed with."

65
00:05:15,125 --> 00:05:17,666
But the call cut out before he'd finished.

66
00:05:17,750 --> 00:05:21,000
There you go. He probably
knew something and was silenced.

67
00:05:21,083 --> 00:05:22,833
Have you seen this person before?

68
00:05:26,583 --> 00:05:27,625
No.

69
00:05:32,750 --> 00:05:33,791
After Zoe's death,

70
00:05:34,708 --> 00:05:36,750
did William do anything strange?

71
00:05:43,208 --> 00:05:47,375
Hey. Think carefully, all right.
Is there anything else?

72
00:05:51,083 --> 00:05:53,791
One time, I helped him
move some dirty cash flow.

73
00:05:53,875 --> 00:05:54,958
Why was that strange?

74
00:05:55,666 --> 00:05:58,583
Because he wanted me
to store the money in a sound wallet.

75
00:05:58,666 --> 00:06:00,750
That's not how we handle cash flow.

76
00:06:01,958 --> 00:06:03,583
Sound wallet.

77
00:06:04,083 --> 00:06:05,833
Any idea who it was for?

78
00:06:05,916 --> 00:06:08,208
I don't know. He told me not to ask.

79
00:06:11,041 --> 00:06:12,875
That's really all I know.

80
00:06:15,708 --> 00:06:18,833
When you get to the airport,
don't make any calls.

81
00:06:18,916 --> 00:06:20,333
Buy the earliest ticket out of here.

82
00:06:21,291 --> 00:06:22,291
You hear me?

83
00:06:27,583 --> 00:06:29,916
Could the person
William said shouldn't be messed with

84
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:33,541
and the person the sound wallet was for
be the same person?

85
00:06:35,541 --> 00:06:38,416
Hey, what's this sound wallet doodad?

86
00:06:39,625 --> 00:06:42,708
Crypto users have a 256-bit private key.

87
00:06:43,208 --> 00:06:45,000
Each one has a recovery phrase.

88
00:06:45,500 --> 00:06:47,291
You write it down, you could lose it.

89
00:06:47,375 --> 00:06:50,125
But storing it on a computer
makes it easy to steal.

90
00:06:50,625 --> 00:06:53,875
You can convert the recovery phrase
into an audio file.

91
00:06:53,958 --> 00:06:56,458
You can access the account
by decoding the audio.

92
00:06:56,541 --> 00:06:58,833
We could trace the money
and find further clues.

93
00:06:59,333 --> 00:07:00,916
As long as we can decode the audio.

94
00:07:02,083 --> 00:07:03,875
Seek and ye shall find.

95
00:07:04,458 --> 00:07:07,000
But don't always trust what you hear.

96
00:07:08,041 --> 00:07:09,291
Now William's dead.

97
00:07:10,333 --> 00:07:13,166
We also don't know
where the sound wallet went.

98
00:07:13,250 --> 00:07:15,791
Why do rich people
have to make things so complicated?

99
00:07:15,875 --> 00:07:20,041
Having to use this damn wallet.
Seeing your money is so much simpler.

100
00:07:20,916 --> 00:07:21,833
Isn't it?

101
00:07:24,958 --> 00:07:26,083
Mina.

102
00:07:26,583 --> 00:07:28,625
You said Gerald gave you your necklace?

103
00:07:40,958 --> 00:07:43,000
Why are you looking into this audio file?

104
00:07:43,500 --> 00:07:45,875
It's best you don't know.

105
00:07:45,958 --> 00:07:47,000
Oh, here we go.

106
00:07:47,083 --> 00:07:49,958
You said you'd buy me a meal
last time. You didn't.

107
00:07:52,541 --> 00:07:54,875
Hey, Taro! Don't go there. I told you.

108
00:07:54,958 --> 00:07:56,833
-You'll just hit someone.
-La, la, la, la, la!

109
00:07:58,166 --> 00:08:01,625
-Does he come here every day?
-Today's a holiday. Kindergarten's closed.

110
00:08:01,708 --> 00:08:04,875
I have to take him out to burn off energy
or he won't sleep at night.

111
00:08:04,958 --> 00:08:06,208
Get him an iPad. It's easier.

112
00:08:06,291 --> 00:08:08,250
An iPad will make him near-sighted.

113
00:08:08,333 --> 00:08:10,625
How about you stop that?
I'll take you to buy an ice cream.

114
00:08:10,708 --> 00:08:13,166
Ice cream has trans fats.
You shouldn't eat it.

115
00:08:15,500 --> 00:08:18,333
Hey. Looks like Gerald
does have a crypto account.

116
00:08:18,416 --> 00:08:20,583
PRIVATE KEY

117
00:08:20,666 --> 00:08:24,083
PRIVATE KEY, UNLOCK WALLET

118
00:08:25,750 --> 00:08:28,041
GERALD CHEN, $3,246,161.82 (UDST)

119
00:08:30,125 --> 00:08:32,041
100 million in Taiwan dollars.

120
00:08:32,125 --> 00:08:34,875
100 million? Holy shit.

121
00:08:34,958 --> 00:08:36,625
He left you that much?

122
00:08:37,125 --> 00:08:40,083
Gerald wouldn't just have left money.

123
00:08:40,583 --> 00:08:42,708
He would have left other clues.

124
00:08:47,875 --> 00:08:50,666
I just traced
Gerald's cryptocurrency account.

125
00:08:50,750 --> 00:08:53,416
There was a large transfer
just before he disappeared.

126
00:08:53,500 --> 00:08:55,250
He bought a house in the mountains.

127
00:08:55,750 --> 00:08:57,791
I'll send the address when I find it.

128
00:09:04,375 --> 00:09:06,083
So he bought a house.

129
00:09:06,583 --> 00:09:08,083
Could he be hiding out there?

130
00:09:14,666 --> 00:09:16,166
I'll come with you tomorrow.

131
00:09:17,625 --> 00:09:19,250
I never said I'd go.

132
00:09:20,083 --> 00:09:24,291
It's possible he might not want you
to get involved.

133
00:09:28,541 --> 00:09:32,291
Gerald and Ben have always been
very protective of me.

134
00:09:34,291 --> 00:09:37,208
But they haven't taken care of themselves.

135
00:09:39,625 --> 00:09:42,416
You think he's out there.

136
00:09:43,083 --> 00:09:44,041
Am I right?

137
00:09:48,166 --> 00:09:50,000
We'll know when we see him.

138
00:09:53,666 --> 00:09:55,333
Hey, eat something.

139
00:09:55,833 --> 00:09:57,000
It's getting cold.

140
00:10:00,583 --> 00:10:02,250
What's with the radish and pork?

141
00:10:02,750 --> 00:10:04,208
I have to eat too.

142
00:10:04,791 --> 00:10:06,583
Why would anyone want to eat that?

143
00:10:07,166 --> 00:10:08,666
You want some? Fried tofu.

144
00:10:08,750 --> 00:10:09,916
The skin's gross. No.

145
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:11,708
You're a child. Try some.

146
00:10:11,791 --> 00:10:12,833
If I have to.

147
00:10:14,875 --> 00:10:16,916
-Mmm.
-That was radish you ate!

148
00:10:17,541 --> 00:10:18,958
-Tofu.
-Show me then.

149
00:10:19,041 --> 00:10:20,375
-Bah.
-Uh!

150
00:10:20,458 --> 00:10:21,375
-Uh.
-Uh.

151
00:10:21,458 --> 00:10:22,708
-I didn't see it.
-Swallowed it.

152
00:10:22,791 --> 00:10:25,250
-You have to eat another one.
-I just ate it.

153
00:10:25,333 --> 00:10:27,833
You obviously ate a radish.
Then eat a blood pudding.

154
00:10:27,916 --> 00:10:30,041
-If you eat a pork meatball.
-Eat this. Here.

155
00:10:30,625 --> 00:10:32,166
Mm. Mm.

156
00:10:32,250 --> 00:10:33,250
Eat some pork.

157
00:10:34,250 --> 00:10:35,916
I'm gonna eat one, all right?

158
00:10:39,083 --> 00:10:40,583
That was obviously tofu.

159
00:10:44,083 --> 00:10:48,250
Hey. Why do you think
Gerald left so much money for Mina?

160
00:10:48,333 --> 00:10:49,541
What's going on there?

161
00:10:49,625 --> 00:10:50,791
AUTHENTIC TIEN-BU-LA

162
00:10:50,875 --> 00:10:51,875
Mina.

163
00:10:52,541 --> 00:10:54,750
-Back then when she stumbled on us…
-Yeah.

164
00:10:54,833 --> 00:10:56,333
…I was going to kill her.

165
00:10:56,833 --> 00:10:58,791
It was Gerald saved her life.

166
00:10:58,875 --> 00:10:59,916
Oh.

167
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:03,208
And then she hung around you guys.
Does she have any family?

168
00:11:03,708 --> 00:11:06,041
-She was a runaway.
-Yeah?

169
00:11:06,125 --> 00:11:09,250
I'd never seen a child that young
who could be so--

170
00:11:09,333 --> 00:11:11,833
-Difficult.
-Stubborn.

171
00:11:13,083 --> 00:11:14,750
-Think so?
-I know so.

172
00:11:14,833 --> 00:11:16,666
-Ah.
-She's not afraid of anything.

173
00:11:17,250 --> 00:11:20,208
It's as if all the worst things
have already happened to her.

174
00:11:20,791 --> 00:11:22,958
So this is why she's how she is.

175
00:11:23,041 --> 00:11:24,083
Ah.

176
00:11:24,166 --> 00:11:26,583
Now I get it. Ah. Very believable.

177
00:11:26,666 --> 00:11:30,916
But after meeting you guys,
she… she's a lot more talkative.

178
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:32,500
-Really?
-Mm.

179
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:33,833
Hey.

180
00:11:34,458 --> 00:11:37,416
Do you think Gerald's still with us?

181
00:11:39,583 --> 00:11:43,500
In our line of work,
you don't get to do it till you retire.

182
00:11:44,083 --> 00:11:45,416
If I hadn't lost this leg,

183
00:11:46,208 --> 00:11:48,291
I wouldn't have made it this far.

184
00:11:48,875 --> 00:11:50,375
What happened to your leg?

185
00:11:50,916 --> 00:11:51,875
Ah.

186
00:11:52,583 --> 00:11:53,916
Failed mission.

187
00:11:54,500 --> 00:11:59,041
Yeh Yueh Tong decided I was useless,
so they let me retire with honor.

188
00:11:59,125 --> 00:12:00,458
That's inhuman.

189
00:12:00,541 --> 00:12:02,666
-Fucking hell.
-Mm.

190
00:12:03,250 --> 00:12:04,291
Hey, listen.

191
00:12:05,208 --> 00:12:08,000
-When I retire, I wanna have a stall.
-Hm.

192
00:12:08,083 --> 00:12:10,916
Specifically swamp eel.
I'll set up next to you.

193
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:12,958
We'd be a one-stop shop. How about it?

194
00:12:13,041 --> 00:12:17,208
Leave me out of it. It'd be crowded.
You wanna do that? Go way over there.

195
00:12:17,291 --> 00:12:19,041
Wouldn't it be nice to have company?

196
00:12:19,125 --> 00:12:22,208
I'm worried you'll be cold and lonely
in your old age.

197
00:12:22,291 --> 00:12:24,000
Hey, hey, hey, hey. Ha, ha.

198
00:12:24,500 --> 00:12:26,166
Ha, ha, ho.

199
00:12:27,208 --> 00:12:28,833
You don't get it. You…

200
00:12:28,916 --> 00:12:31,125
-Drink your soup.
-I'm good.

201
00:12:31,208 --> 00:12:33,125
-Deep-fried tofu?
-No, really.

202
00:12:33,208 --> 00:12:35,500
-I'm home.
-Are you now?

203
00:12:35,583 --> 00:12:37,541
-You haven't gone to bed yet.
-No.

204
00:12:37,625 --> 00:12:38,958
Uh, where's Howie?

205
00:12:39,041 --> 00:12:41,666
-Doing homework in his room.
-Ah. I got you a snack.

206
00:12:41,750 --> 00:12:43,458
Tien-bu-la with blood pudding.

207
00:12:43,958 --> 00:12:45,083
-Oh.
-Hm.

208
00:12:45,166 --> 00:12:48,250
Howie! Your father brought
a midnight snack.

209
00:12:48,333 --> 00:12:49,333
Come and eat.

210
00:12:50,625 --> 00:12:52,125
-Hey, hold on.
-Yeah?

211
00:12:53,708 --> 00:12:55,000
What's in the bag?

212
00:12:57,666 --> 00:13:01,708
Ah. Young Gold thought I needed
new clothes, so he bought me these.

213
00:13:01,791 --> 00:13:04,291
-Ah, your boss treats you so well.
-Mm.

214
00:13:04,375 --> 00:13:05,666
Handsome and generous.

215
00:13:05,750 --> 00:13:07,750
Invite him over for dinner
when he gets time.

216
00:13:07,833 --> 00:13:09,583
-Great. Will do, will do.
-Good.

217
00:13:24,125 --> 00:13:26,291
What do you call this?
Why are you shutting your door?

218
00:13:27,250 --> 00:13:28,541
I was about to take a shower.

219
00:13:28,625 --> 00:13:30,166
You're so sneaky.

220
00:13:30,250 --> 00:13:32,416
-Out of the way.
-I know you're up to something.

221
00:13:33,833 --> 00:13:35,083
Seriously.

222
00:13:50,125 --> 00:13:51,375
Oh!

223
00:14:04,083 --> 00:14:05,666
You're in a good mood.

224
00:14:05,750 --> 00:14:08,541
I was thinking about
what your dad got for my last birthday.

225
00:14:08,625 --> 00:14:11,333
-Was that the fill light?
-That's right.

226
00:14:11,416 --> 00:14:13,250
And the message was something like,

227
00:14:13,333 --> 00:14:17,083
"Wendy Wu, beautiful as a fairy,
thanks to this light."

228
00:14:17,166 --> 00:14:19,125
-It sucked.
-He always gets it wrong.

229
00:14:19,708 --> 00:14:22,416
I have to say, your father,

230
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:25,250
he's got it right this time.

231
00:14:28,791 --> 00:14:29,791
Madame Fan.

232
00:14:31,250 --> 00:14:32,666
They found Gerald.

233
00:14:36,416 --> 00:14:38,000
Make sure they're not alerted.

234
00:14:38,791 --> 00:14:41,208
Get fixers to keep watch.

235
00:14:41,916 --> 00:14:44,583
Anything happens, report back.

236
00:14:45,083 --> 00:14:46,083
Okay.

237
00:14:46,666 --> 00:14:50,583
While he's still alive,
we won't be able to face our client.

238
00:14:51,083 --> 00:14:52,375
You know what to do.

239
00:14:54,541 --> 00:14:56,416
I want it clean.

240
00:14:57,541 --> 00:15:00,041
Yeh Yueh Tong can't be implicated.

241
00:15:00,541 --> 00:15:01,833
No problem.

242
00:15:17,125 --> 00:15:19,958
-Yeah?
-I have some things to do at home.

243
00:15:20,041 --> 00:15:22,000
I won't be coming over
to third wheel today.

244
00:15:23,125 --> 00:15:24,166
You're a slacker.

245
00:15:24,250 --> 00:15:26,625
This cool autumn weather
is perfect for an outing.

246
00:15:26,708 --> 00:15:28,625
Take advantage of the opportunity, okay?

247
00:15:28,708 --> 00:15:29,708
-Bye-bye.
-Hey!

248
00:15:53,083 --> 00:15:56,291
When you're in the States,
if you need money, just tell me.

249
00:15:56,375 --> 00:15:58,708
I hear that things
are super expensive there.

250
00:15:58,791 --> 00:16:00,500
Don't suffer. There's no need to be proud.

251
00:16:00,583 --> 00:16:02,750
Don't worry.
You've already given me enough.

252
00:16:02,833 --> 00:16:04,583
And I've applied for a job there.

253
00:16:05,083 --> 00:16:06,333
So I can pay you back later.

254
00:16:06,416 --> 00:16:08,791
It's just what I owed your father before.

255
00:16:08,875 --> 00:16:10,041
Felix.

256
00:16:10,125 --> 00:16:11,333
Listen to me.

257
00:16:11,416 --> 00:16:14,041
You've been taking care of me
all these years.

258
00:16:14,125 --> 00:16:16,958
When mom was sick, you helped out.
It's my turn.

259
00:16:19,541 --> 00:16:22,333
Ah, you shouldn't be worrying about money.
Focus on study.

260
00:16:22,416 --> 00:16:24,458
Hey, I'll take you to the airport
in the morning.

261
00:16:24,958 --> 00:16:27,083
It's all right.
I've already booked a ride.

262
00:16:32,458 --> 00:16:33,583
-Hey.
-Yeah?

263
00:16:33,666 --> 00:16:35,666
This is for you on behalf of your dad.

264
00:16:37,416 --> 00:16:41,458
Your dad's greatest wish
was to send you abroad to study.

265
00:16:41,958 --> 00:16:44,666
And for you to see the world.
Now I've helped him fulfil it.

266
00:16:46,916 --> 00:16:47,916
Help me out.

267
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:49,791
Oh. Here we are.

268
00:16:52,208 --> 00:16:53,500
From now on,

269
00:16:53,583 --> 00:16:55,458
when you're wearing this,

270
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:58,250
It'll be like…

271
00:16:58,791 --> 00:17:01,083
It'll be like
your dad's right next to you.

272
00:17:04,500 --> 00:17:06,166
Okay, done.

273
00:17:08,708 --> 00:17:10,375
I'll come back to visit you.

274
00:17:11,750 --> 00:17:12,958
Look after yourself.

275
00:17:17,916 --> 00:17:20,375
Ah. Don't cry.

276
00:17:20,458 --> 00:17:22,583
When you cry, you're uglier than your dad.

277
00:17:22,666 --> 00:17:25,291
Why do you always have to do that?

278
00:17:25,375 --> 00:17:27,875
-You're so annoying.
-I'm gonna go pee.

279
00:17:27,958 --> 00:17:28,958
Huh?

280
00:17:29,041 --> 00:17:30,500
You're so weird.

281
00:17:41,375 --> 00:17:43,250
Why are you stepping down so suddenly?

282
00:17:44,250 --> 00:17:46,958
Is there someone you'd like to nominate?

283
00:17:50,791 --> 00:17:52,333
I've gotten too old for this.

284
00:17:52,416 --> 00:17:54,541
It's time I stepped down.

285
00:17:54,625 --> 00:17:56,458
While the step's still there,

286
00:17:56,958 --> 00:17:58,750
stepping down's very easy.

287
00:17:58,833 --> 00:18:01,166
If you wait till the step's taken away,

288
00:18:01,666 --> 00:18:04,916
no matter how you do it,
you're gonna get hurt.

289
00:18:05,916 --> 00:18:06,833
Terra,

290
00:18:08,375 --> 00:18:10,083
this is a heavy step.

291
00:18:10,916 --> 00:18:13,541
It will take a lot of people to move it.

292
00:18:15,041 --> 00:18:17,583
There are a lot of people
who wanna move it.

293
00:18:20,208 --> 00:18:22,208
Like father, like daughter.

294
00:18:24,166 --> 00:18:27,000
And this outsider has a lot of support.

295
00:18:27,083 --> 00:18:30,208
They outnumber the insider support.

296
00:18:32,916 --> 00:18:36,333
I'm old. I can't get involved anymore.

297
00:18:43,166 --> 00:18:44,458
Old friend,

298
00:18:45,958 --> 00:18:48,375
I hope you get to leave on a high note.

299
00:18:48,875 --> 00:18:50,708
I'll have the tea waiting.

300
00:18:59,250 --> 00:19:02,875
THE TIMES ARE AGAINST ME. WHAT CAN I DO?

301
00:19:04,833 --> 00:19:05,875
Excuse me.

302
00:19:06,375 --> 00:19:09,416
Can you please
interpret this fortune stick for me?

303
00:19:11,958 --> 00:19:15,250
"Your path to fame is not yet clear,

304
00:19:15,333 --> 00:19:18,000
with stormy clashes drawing near."

305
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:22,166
"Guard both sides from pain and loss."

306
00:19:23,208 --> 00:19:27,458
"Relax, sigh not
and wait your toss." There.

307
00:19:28,500 --> 00:19:31,541
Are you asking
for family, luck, or career?

308
00:19:31,625 --> 00:19:33,708
Madam Fan got it for you.

309
00:19:54,750 --> 00:19:55,583
Yes?

310
00:20:10,041 --> 00:20:12,083
We go up this path and we're there.

311
00:20:12,166 --> 00:20:14,208
LIEN HSIN BRIDGE

312
00:21:15,375 --> 00:21:17,125
He's probably after the same thing.

313
00:21:17,208 --> 00:21:18,833
It's Yeh Yueh Tong's fixer.

314
00:21:19,333 --> 00:21:21,375
Madam Fan knows they've found Gerald.

315
00:21:23,708 --> 00:21:24,541
Come on.

316
00:22:05,583 --> 00:22:06,833
Excuse me.

317
00:22:07,833 --> 00:22:09,208
Have you seen this person?

318
00:22:12,416 --> 00:22:13,458
Thank you.

319
00:22:20,791 --> 00:22:24,541
All branches have been notified
of the time of the secret meeting.

320
00:22:25,375 --> 00:22:26,333
Mm.

321
00:22:27,708 --> 00:22:29,416
The gods have spoken.

322
00:22:29,500 --> 00:22:31,041
I drew Lot 28.

323
00:22:31,625 --> 00:22:34,250
"The golden days of old have nearly gone."

324
00:22:34,333 --> 00:22:36,875
"A mighty tiger now stranded and drawn."

325
00:22:36,958 --> 00:22:38,708
"Fortune is fickle, fey, and fleet."

326
00:22:39,500 --> 00:22:42,208
"So seize the hour before it flees."

327
00:22:44,666 --> 00:22:46,875
You recall the stories behind this slip?

328
00:22:48,125 --> 00:22:52,833
One was Cao Cao's capture
after meeting Zhang Xiu in Wancheng.

329
00:22:53,416 --> 00:22:54,958
The other was Xiang Yu,

330
00:22:55,041 --> 00:22:59,625
who, defeated and surrounded by enemies
at Wu River, decided to end it.

331
00:23:00,125 --> 00:23:03,125
Mm. One was betrayed,

332
00:23:03,625 --> 00:23:07,208
yet was able to escape danger
and achieve dominance.

333
00:23:08,208 --> 00:23:10,583
The other, a hero who lost faith.

334
00:23:11,166 --> 00:23:13,125
He'd reached the end of the line.

335
00:23:14,666 --> 00:23:15,500
Hey.

336
00:23:15,583 --> 00:23:16,458
Which one,

337
00:23:17,333 --> 00:23:18,500
in your opinion,

338
00:23:18,583 --> 00:23:20,166
Is the slip about?

339
00:23:21,041 --> 00:23:24,291
This depends on whether
the individual concerned

340
00:23:24,375 --> 00:23:27,541
can adapt
and humble themselves to survive.

341
00:23:31,583 --> 00:23:32,583
You're right.

342
00:23:34,375 --> 00:23:36,375
Am I needed for anything else?

343
00:23:36,458 --> 00:23:38,166
No. Thank you.

344
00:23:38,833 --> 00:23:41,458
You've been working so hard
for Ching He lately.

345
00:23:41,541 --> 00:23:44,000
Take a few days off. Get some rest.

346
00:23:50,208 --> 00:23:52,916
You let Gold go along to find Gerald.

347
00:23:53,416 --> 00:23:57,500
If he learns the truth, don't you fear
what the consequences will be?

348
00:24:00,916 --> 00:24:02,875
If it's something he needed to know,

349
00:24:02,958 --> 00:24:05,000
someone would have told him soon enough.

350
00:24:06,791 --> 00:24:09,833
I fear this decision was made in haste.

351
00:24:11,125 --> 00:24:13,166
Once some things are known,

352
00:24:13,916 --> 00:24:15,458
there is no going back.

353
00:24:17,791 --> 00:24:18,875
Hm.

354
00:24:28,541 --> 00:24:30,500
The garden looks cared for.

355
00:24:32,041 --> 00:24:33,458
There's someone around.

356
00:25:07,791 --> 00:25:10,291
Zoe?

357
00:25:12,541 --> 00:25:14,458
Hey.

358
00:25:14,541 --> 00:25:15,541
What do you want?

359
00:25:16,500 --> 00:25:17,500
Stay there.

360
00:25:18,250 --> 00:25:19,666
Just put the gun down.

361
00:25:20,166 --> 00:25:21,375
Don't hurt your child.

362
00:25:21,458 --> 00:25:23,041
Stay there.

363
00:25:27,666 --> 00:25:28,625
Why?

364
00:25:29,500 --> 00:25:31,208
Why won't you leave me alone?

365
00:25:31,291 --> 00:25:34,541
We won't hurt you.
We're here for Gerald Chen.

366
00:25:39,166 --> 00:25:40,875
He went AWOL a year ago

367
00:25:40,958 --> 00:25:43,833
and left us a clue to find him here.

368
00:25:53,625 --> 00:25:55,458
You're the one in the photo.

369
00:26:29,750 --> 00:26:30,708
You and Gerald.

370
00:26:31,708 --> 00:26:33,166
What was your relationship?

371
00:26:41,250 --> 00:26:43,375
He was the one who came to kill me.

372
00:26:52,750 --> 00:26:53,833
Are you here yet?

373
00:26:54,333 --> 00:26:55,500
I'm not coming.

374
00:26:56,333 --> 00:26:57,541
Don't contact me again.

375
00:26:57,625 --> 00:26:59,500
Wait. William!

376
00:26:59,583 --> 00:27:00,541
Hello?

377
00:27:19,666 --> 00:27:23,250
When he saw that I was pregnant.
He couldn't go through with it.

378
00:27:26,916 --> 00:27:28,541
If Gerald didn't finish the job,

379
00:27:29,125 --> 00:27:32,125
Yeh Yueh Tong wouldn't spare him,
and you wouldn't still be here.

380
00:27:33,875 --> 00:27:35,708
That's why we faked my death.

381
00:27:47,583 --> 00:27:49,083
We fooled everyone.

382
00:27:51,916 --> 00:27:53,041
Target Zoe

383
00:27:53,541 --> 00:27:54,708
confirmed dead.

384
00:27:58,333 --> 00:27:59,916
Why are you helping me?

385
00:28:00,875 --> 00:28:02,125
I don't wanna fuck up again.

386
00:28:05,416 --> 00:28:07,041
Then he brought me here to lie low.

387
00:28:08,250 --> 00:28:09,541
So, where's he?

388
00:28:12,125 --> 00:28:13,291
GERALD CHEN

389
00:28:15,375 --> 00:28:16,208
Yes?

390
00:28:16,291 --> 00:28:18,208
I might not be able to get there again.

391
00:28:18,291 --> 00:28:20,458
There's a bag of cash in the ceiling.

392
00:28:20,541 --> 00:28:22,500
Enough for you and your daughter.

393
00:28:22,583 --> 00:28:23,708
Once things calm down--

394
00:28:25,125 --> 00:28:25,958
Wait.

395
00:28:27,041 --> 00:28:27,916
Wait.

396
00:28:30,291 --> 00:28:31,250
You there?

397
00:28:32,166 --> 00:28:33,916
That was the last time he called.

398
00:28:40,375 --> 00:28:41,583
He could be dead.

399
00:28:41,666 --> 00:28:42,833
He's not.

400
00:28:42,916 --> 00:28:45,166
He would have planned everything.

401
00:28:46,208 --> 00:28:49,958
He probably knew his life was in danger
when he was sent to kill me.

402
00:28:52,625 --> 00:28:53,750
What do you mean?

403
00:28:57,750 --> 00:29:00,041
Before accepting the mission,
Gerald must have known

404
00:29:00,125 --> 00:29:03,416
that Yeh Yueh Tong would eliminate him
to protect this secret.

405
00:29:13,166 --> 00:29:15,208
Why does Yeh Yueh Tong wanna kill you?

406
00:29:16,625 --> 00:29:19,291
What's so important
so many people need to die?

407
00:29:26,500 --> 00:29:27,541
Your family.

408
00:29:28,416 --> 00:29:29,625
What do you mean?

409
00:29:30,208 --> 00:29:31,583
The Hsueh clan.

410
00:29:32,916 --> 00:29:33,916
They killed my husband.

411
00:29:34,875 --> 00:29:36,500
And would have killed me and my daughter.

412
00:29:37,708 --> 00:29:39,041
We were fortunate.

413
00:29:39,541 --> 00:29:41,541
I'd happily take all of you with me.

414
00:29:41,625 --> 00:29:43,791
-Why does the Hsueh clan--
-Don't come any closer!

415
00:29:52,208 --> 00:29:54,166
Anyway, a life for a life.

416
00:29:54,250 --> 00:29:56,250
That's some justice.

417
00:29:56,333 --> 00:29:57,500
Just calm down.

418
00:29:58,166 --> 00:30:00,708
Why did my family
kill William and your husband?

419
00:30:01,291 --> 00:30:02,625
What's it all for?

420
00:30:05,375 --> 00:30:07,708
Do you honestly have no idea?

421
00:30:08,291 --> 00:30:10,916
The Hsin Nan redevelopment zone
is so huge.

422
00:30:11,000 --> 00:30:14,375
It was approved so quickly. That wouldn't
have happened without your family.

423
00:30:15,500 --> 00:30:18,750
William helped them launder the money.
You must have known that.

424
00:30:35,000 --> 00:30:36,916
I just want us to be safe.

425
00:30:37,000 --> 00:30:40,458
Pretend that I'm dead. I'm not gonna talk.

426
00:30:42,958 --> 00:30:44,000
Don't worry.

427
00:30:44,791 --> 00:30:46,208
We won't tell anyone.

428
00:30:55,708 --> 00:30:57,958
Happy birthday to you

429
00:30:58,041 --> 00:31:00,458
Happy birthday to you

430
00:31:00,541 --> 00:31:05,500
Happy birthday, dear Wendy
Happy birthday to you

431
00:31:05,583 --> 00:31:07,750
Yay! Blow out the candles.

432
00:31:08,333 --> 00:31:09,916
Yay!

433
00:31:10,000 --> 00:31:11,833
Mom, here you are.

434
00:31:11,916 --> 00:31:15,416
Oh, you're such a good son. Thank you.

435
00:31:15,500 --> 00:31:18,333
Hey, your husband's
pretty amazing as well.

436
00:31:19,458 --> 00:31:20,458
Thank you.

437
00:31:20,541 --> 00:31:21,583
MOM

438
00:31:22,083 --> 00:31:23,416
Perfume?

439
00:31:23,500 --> 00:31:27,083
Oh yeah. Hey, do you remember
when you were pregnant with Howie?

440
00:31:27,583 --> 00:31:28,833
We were at the shopping center,

441
00:31:28,916 --> 00:31:31,958
and you smelled this scent
and you really wanted it,

442
00:31:32,041 --> 00:31:34,208
and you couldn't
bring yourself to buy it, hm?

443
00:31:41,416 --> 00:31:43,291
-Felix.
-Hm?

444
00:31:43,375 --> 00:31:46,166
A husband and wife
can tell each other anything, right?

445
00:31:46,250 --> 00:31:47,375
Mm.

446
00:31:47,958 --> 00:31:49,875
Are you hiding something?

447
00:31:50,666 --> 00:31:53,291
What would I be hiding?

448
00:31:53,791 --> 00:31:55,500
Ah, you're imagining things.

449
00:31:55,583 --> 00:31:57,291
Go to sleep, will you, okay?

450
00:31:57,791 --> 00:31:58,833
Are you sure?

451
00:31:59,958 --> 00:32:01,250
Yes, really.

452
00:32:03,333 --> 00:32:05,916
You are so weird.

453
00:32:13,125 --> 00:32:15,125
The kid hasn't spilled, has he?

454
00:32:16,291 --> 00:32:17,291
What did you say?

455
00:32:17,375 --> 00:32:19,458
Oh, it was nothing,

456
00:32:19,541 --> 00:32:22,291
Nothing. Go to sleep
and don't dream, will you?

457
00:32:22,791 --> 00:32:24,625
Off to sleep now.

458
00:32:30,500 --> 00:32:32,125
From the exam results,

459
00:32:33,500 --> 00:32:37,250
it looks like
Mr. Hsueh's liver cancer has metastasized.

460
00:32:37,333 --> 00:32:39,625
He should begin treatment
as soon as possible.

461
00:32:42,291 --> 00:32:43,875
Okay, I understand.

462
00:32:44,375 --> 00:32:47,000
Doctor, this news must be kept secret.

463
00:32:47,500 --> 00:32:48,333
All right.

464
00:32:55,416 --> 00:32:58,625
My illness might be of benefit to you.

465
00:33:00,541 --> 00:33:03,541
Look. Pick the right time
to announce it to the public.

466
00:33:05,500 --> 00:33:07,083
The timing is critical.

467
00:33:08,625 --> 00:33:11,041
There can be no errors. You got that?

468
00:33:11,666 --> 00:33:12,500
Mm.

469
00:33:17,125 --> 00:33:18,250
And also,

470
00:33:19,458 --> 00:33:21,208
you can't tell your brother yet.

471
00:33:23,875 --> 00:33:24,833
Okay.

472
00:33:26,958 --> 00:33:28,125
Dad,

473
00:33:29,041 --> 00:33:30,375
get some rest.

474
00:33:49,375 --> 00:33:51,166
The situation's changed.

475
00:33:55,875 --> 00:33:59,583
I always thought
that if we kept searching…

476
00:34:01,750 --> 00:34:03,250
then he was still with us.

477
00:34:09,083 --> 00:34:10,875
He left you the necklace.

478
00:34:11,958 --> 00:34:13,416
Perhaps he hoped, one day,

479
00:34:14,375 --> 00:34:16,041
that you'd meet up at that house.

480
00:34:19,750 --> 00:34:21,708
He knew he was going to die.

481
00:34:21,791 --> 00:34:26,000
That's why he left the necklace for me
before carrying out the mission.

482
00:34:26,958 --> 00:34:29,750
But he never expected you
to join Yeh Yueh Tong.

483
00:34:31,083 --> 00:34:32,416
What are you going to do?

484
00:34:33,541 --> 00:34:36,333
Madam Fan's kept me close all this time

485
00:34:36,416 --> 00:34:38,625
just so she can track down Gerald.

486
00:34:48,000 --> 00:34:49,125
What is it?

487
00:34:52,291 --> 00:34:53,958
The fact Zoe's alive

488
00:34:54,458 --> 00:34:56,791
isn't just bad for Yeh Yueh Tong.

489
00:34:58,166 --> 00:34:59,541
It's also a threat

490
00:35:00,500 --> 00:35:01,875
to the Hsueh clan.

491
00:35:01,958 --> 00:35:03,041
I won't hurt her.

492
00:35:03,125 --> 00:35:04,833
I know you won't do that.

493
00:35:07,041 --> 00:35:08,791
At least not at the moment.

494
00:35:09,291 --> 00:35:10,291
Meaning?

495
00:35:11,541 --> 00:35:15,416
I can't predict
what you could do just to score points.

496
00:35:15,916 --> 00:35:17,125
From the very beginning,

497
00:35:19,041 --> 00:35:21,166
I was used by you to find her.

498
00:35:21,750 --> 00:35:22,916
Isn't that right?

499
00:35:29,000 --> 00:35:31,625
Ching He
is holding a secret meeting today.

500
00:35:31,708 --> 00:35:33,916
The six leaders will be there.

501
00:35:36,083 --> 00:35:39,458
No doubt there'll be fireworks.

502
00:35:46,166 --> 00:35:47,875
TERRA

503
00:35:47,958 --> 00:35:51,083
Terra has always been on time.

504
00:35:51,583 --> 00:35:52,708
What's going on today?

505
00:35:52,791 --> 00:35:53,625
EARTH

506
00:35:56,208 --> 00:35:58,916
Oh, what a pity.

507
00:35:59,666 --> 00:36:01,333
There'll be an apology.

508
00:36:04,666 --> 00:36:05,500
Everyone…

509
00:36:08,958 --> 00:36:09,791
Chairman,

510
00:36:10,875 --> 00:36:12,458
Terra won't be coming.

511
00:36:14,375 --> 00:36:18,291
Terra was found dead in the suburbs.

512
00:36:22,125 --> 00:36:23,625
How could this happen?

513
00:36:25,208 --> 00:36:27,916
We should adjourn.

514
00:36:29,125 --> 00:36:32,333
We will resume
after I've investigated Terra's death.

515
00:36:33,791 --> 00:36:34,875
Chairman,

516
00:36:35,958 --> 00:36:39,333
we should take our time discussing

517
00:36:39,916 --> 00:36:42,375
If there are better candidates

518
00:36:42,458 --> 00:36:44,958
for the position of Fixer Celestial.

519
00:36:47,875 --> 00:36:49,250
What do you mean by that?

520
00:36:50,250 --> 00:36:55,458
The Hong family, for generations,
have served Ching He well.

521
00:36:56,041 --> 00:37:00,083
Everything we do
is in Ching He's best interests.

522
00:37:01,625 --> 00:37:04,458
Ching He has stood strong for 100 years

523
00:37:04,958 --> 00:37:09,416
because of leaders who know
how to adapt to changing circumstances

524
00:37:09,500 --> 00:37:11,250
and make the best choice.

525
00:37:12,708 --> 00:37:17,416
Sir Hong's already agreed to hand over
the key to Kuang Ming Chamber.

526
00:37:17,500 --> 00:37:19,208
But the chair,

527
